   "line": [
    "Nxe4"
   ],
   "spoken": "After the main-line exchanges we have three good replies — the bishop to f5, the knight to d7, or the knight to f6.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "the three Caro-Kann main replies"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 833.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/8/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 5",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight to f6 is the Tartakower — it accepts a slightly damaged pawn structure in return for solid, active piece play. Once the least popular of the three, it's now among the most popular.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "the Tartakower: structure for activity"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 841.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/3PN3/5P2/PPP3PP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "f3"
   ],
   "spoken": "White's f3 is premature — it weakens the king far too early.",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 867,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/5b2/3PN3/5P2/PPP3PP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Bf5"
   ],
   "spoken": "We develop with the bishop to f5, pressuring the knight. No need to rush to punish f3 — it's not a race, and White pays for it later.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "develop first; the weakness keeps"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 883.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/5b2/2BPN3/5P2/PPP3PP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [
    "Bc4"
   ],
   "spoken": "White's bishop to c4 tempts us to capture on e4, but taking there is risky — it opens the f-file and hands White real compensation. So we simply keep developing.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "don’t grab a pawn that opens a file at you"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 942,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/5b2/2BPN3/5P2/PPP3PP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 3 7",
   "line": [
    "Nbd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight to d7 is the ideal Caro-Kann arrangement — some players are allergic to the square, but this knight pair is excellent here.",
   "kind": "main",
   "teaches": [
    "the ...Nbd7 setup"
   ]
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 952.5,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp1npppp/2p2n2/5bN1/2BP4/5P2/PPP3PP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 4 7",
   "line": [
    "Ng5"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight to g5 threatens mate.",
   "kind": "main"
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 961,
   "fen": "r2qkb1r/pp1n1ppp/2p1pn2/5bN1/2BP4/5P2/PPP3PP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Which is the perfect moment for e6, blunting the bishop.",
